  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.8,
      "end_seconds": 8.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "doctor, the patient's with us now i did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.32,
      "end_seconds": 15.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "thank you right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.41,
      "end_seconds": 21.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.46,
      "end_seconds": 30.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "I wanted to get severe pain in the upper tummy going through to the back looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 32.83,
      "end_seconds": 45.42,
      "duration_seconds": 12.59,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Weight 83 kilos, pulse 114. Height 185 centimetres, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temperature 36.8, BMI works out to 24.3, blood pressure 127 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.05,
      "end_seconds": 50.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.14,
      "end_seconds": 66.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.23,
      "end_seconds": 79.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "It usually comes with a fast heart. The fast heart? That's been for about two weeks. I've also been feeling very unwell."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.89,
      "end_seconds": 82.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "So, how about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.5,
      "end_seconds": 86.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "no, no fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 88.04,
      "end_seconds": 92.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.68,
      "end_seconds": 101.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.7,
      "end_seconds": 111.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed any black stools, chest pain or yellow eyes at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.25,
      "end_seconds": 117.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "no, no black stools, chest pain or yellow eyes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.25,
      "end_seconds": 122.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.54,
      "end_seconds": 126.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.31,
      "end_seconds": 129.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.12,
      "end_seconds": 134.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "nothing on the the skin, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.32,
      "end_seconds": 138.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.6,
      "end_seconds": 148.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 149.24,
      "end_seconds": 154.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.07,
      "end_seconds": 159.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.28,
      "end_seconds": 168.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.47,
      "end_seconds": 173.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "hm, okay. Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.32,
      "end_seconds": 177.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin. I've got anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.16,
      "end_seconds": 180.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.58,
      "end_seconds": 198.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Okay, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.2,
      "end_seconds": 216.76,
      "duration_seconds": 17.56,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I have about eight cigarettes in a day. I work in accounts at a hospital. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.76,
      "end_seconds": 221.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.37,
      "end_seconds": 235.53,
      "duration_seconds": 13.16,
      "text": "I'm allergic to wheat, I get itchy skin. Yes, plasters. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.37,
      "end_seconds": 242.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.1,
      "end_seconds": 244.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.25,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.93,
      "end_seconds": 265.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "your upper tummy is very tender and you look dehydrated"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.52,
      "end_seconds": 268.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "yes, that's fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.27,
      "end_seconds": 272.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "that's the examination finished"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.16,
      "end_seconds": 294.47,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is acute pancreatitis. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. A perforated ulcer is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.27,
      "end_seconds": 297.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.59,
      "end_seconds": 320.54,
      "duration_seconds": 21.95,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's acute pancreatitis, and we'll know more once the an amylase blood test is back. I think an amylase blood test makes sense here, for severe abdominal pain. I'll request an abdominal scan, it'll help with pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.38,
      "end_seconds": 322.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Mm, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.1,
      "end_seconds": 356.28,
      "duration_seconds": 32.18,
      "text": "You need admission for fluids and pain relief, nothing to eat for now. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. We'll refer you to the surgical team. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's plan a check straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.61,
      "end_seconds": 360.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "erm, good, I'll return then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.69,
      "end_seconds": 365.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "So, have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.98,
      "end_seconds": 369.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.92,
      "end_seconds": 375.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "take care now"
    }
  ]
}